Done. Here's a summary of what was implemented:

**`sessions.py`**
- `CACHE_PATH = STATE_DIR / "_cache.json"` — flat cache alongside the per-repo YAMLs
- `_cache_is_fresh()` — mtime comparison: cache exists and is newer than every `*.yaml`
- `_write_cache()` — serialises `id`, `name`, `profile`, `repo_label`, `repo_path` to JSON
- `_load_cache()` — deserialises back to `Session` objects (missing fields get dataclass defaults)
- `load_sessions_fast()` — serves from cache if fresh, otherwise falls back to `load_sessions` and writes cache

**`cli.py`**
- `--resume` path now uses `load_sessions_fast` (single JSON read on cache hit vs N YAML reads)
- `reindex` command deletes `CACHE_PATH` after rebuilding all indexes

**`indexer.py`**
- `build_index` deletes `CACHE_PATH` after writing the YAML, covering programmatic callers

**Tests** — 5 new tests in `tests/test_resume_cache.py`; all 91 tests pass.
